  note: what does "the sum over the subgroup of" apply to: read as sg_add(lane) * ..., not sg_add(lane * ...) (say "the sum over the subgroup of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(lane: u32 in 0..31) = sg_add(lane)*2
  ucas: show it
it(lane: u32 in 0..31) = 992
